comments.message:
Can we make an enum for this:
enum class DateFormat {
   UTC,
   LocalTimezone,
}

That's a lot more clear than a bool.  Also, lets make it explicit which one we're requesting and avoid the default argument.  There's only a few calls to getDateTimeOffsetNow, making this not a default arg will ensure that we've corrected every place we need to.  As written, things like the Redfish journal will now be incorrect after this change, and still report UTC.
